3368               /TABLE OF VECTORS FOR STANDARD CHARACTER SET.
3369               /EACH 12-BIT WORD CONTAINS ALL THE INFORMATION FOR THE NEXT VECTOR.
3370               /THE CHARACTER CELL IS A 10 X 14 MATRIX WITH 4 ADDITIONAL BLANK SPACES TO THE RIGHT
3371               /OF THE CELL AND 8 ADDITIONAL BLANK SPAAES ABOVE THE CELL (I.E., THE SPACE BETWEEN CELLS
3372               /IN THE SAME LINE IS 4 RASTER UNITS AND THE SPACE BETWEEN LINES IS 8 RASTER UNITS).
3373               /THE BEAM (OR PEN) IS ASSUMED AT THE LOWER LEFT CORNER OF THE CHARACTER CELL INITIALLY,
3374               /AND THE BEAM (OR PEN) MUST BE PUT AT THE LOWER LEFT CORNER OF THE NEXT
3375               /CHARACTER CELL AT THE COMPLETION OF THE PRESENT CHARACTER.  EACH 12-BIT WORD IS
3376               /CONSTRUCTED AS FOLLOWS:
3377               /
3378               /       BIT 00          SET IF THIS IS THE FIRST VECTOR OF A CHARACTER
3379               /       BITS 01-04      X COORDINATE OF TIP COMPARED TO TAIL, I.E., RELATIVE X COMPONENT
3380               /       BIT 05          SET IF X COMPONENT OF VECTOR IS NEGATIVE
3381               /       BIT 06          SET IF VECTOR IS NOT TO BE DISPLAYED OR DRAWN, I.E., DARK VECTOR
3382               /       BITS 07-10      Y COORDINATE OF TIP COMPARED TO TAIL, I.E., RELATIVE Y COMPONENT
3383               /       BIT 11          SET IF Y COMPONENT OF VECTOR IS NEGATIVE
3384               /
3385               
